hi there happy new year  steve here steve kaufman to talk about  language learning  and today i'm going to talk about the  importance of novelty of new things it's  a new year and why we need new things  when we learn languages or maybe other  things as well  2018  wow you know i remember when i was uh  i guess a teenager we had  the novel 1984 by george orwell  and  seemed like a long way into the future  and here we are 2018.  new novelty um i often refer  to a book  by  manfred spitzer  okay  called learning  unfortunately  brain research and the school of  learning of life school of life  he said in there something that i think  is quite profound and it affects  language learning and that is that the  brain needs and he's a brain surgeon  he's a neurosurgeon cognitive sort of  science and stuff the brain needs  repetition  but it needs novelty  okay we need new things we can't just  keep repeating  studying the same material  um  you know robert bjork of ucla has a  bunch of videos where he talks about  interleaving where  you know if you block learn if you try  to learn this one  thing  eventually  this sort of law of diminishing returns  sets in you're learning less and less we  need novelty so  the one thing i because i've been  studying i have these 10 mini stories uh  in link which i've been studying and  listening to i've listened to them 30 40  times re-read them and and still the  same places i don't understand i don't i  read it wrong again and so forth  but  today  uh we uploaded another 20 stories many  stories into link  because i don't control that this is  done by  our collaborator zoran in serbia who has  found someone on upwork which is a  outsourcing website to translate these  stories and record them in arabic and  she by the way is doing a wonderful job  and so another 20 were loaded up i just  got started so even though i haven't  mastered the first 10 stories  the idea i'm like a kid in a candy store  now i've got these news stories that i  can go in and pick my way through and  listen and  and you know as i work my way through  these and again i'll not understand and  whatever but all the while i'm exposing  myself to the language and gradually  everything becomes clearer gradually the  writing system becomes clearer more  words start to stick  and i often remind myself you know what  you know i'm as as much as i'm  determined to sort of learn these 10  stories and  try to get better at them and even not  master them but at least understand more  of them  and i am understanding more but i'm not  moving as fast as i would like then i  remind myself you have to interject  you have to inject rather some novelty  so  at that even a couple of days ago i said  okay  i have  got a sense of the arabic alphabet let's  see how it all works in farsi and some  years ago i bought this  um living language uh farsi course so i  started listening to a bit of pharisee  of course i don't understand a thing and  started reading the first few lessons  here  uh it's  just to see for example the arabic  alphabet with a different language it  interjects injects rather some novelty  and i know i'm going to continue on to  farsi later on  but now that i have the new stories  uh at link i will you know i may just  put my i might still every so often have  a peek at farsi but i will stay with the  news stories but the important thing  there is is to in inject novelty get  some things in there that are new  that stir up the brain the brain likes  to be stimulated and to some extent if  we keep on  sort of plowing the same  furrows in the field  after a while we're not we're not  achieving anything so very important by  the way not everything new is good  i had a look at the the newer version of  this living language  and it is much worse than this one which  was published in 2007  for whatever reason living language has  completely dumbed down their language  courses lots of pictures and stuff like  this and so i certainly will 